Hal Finney makes some thoughtful comments on my "Go" example, though I
disagree with his conclusions. (But then the whole constellation of
"information," "complexity," "entropy," and "randomness" ideas is notorious
for producing varying reactions. This is seen in this recent debate, in
debates in general about entropy and complexity, and in at least a dozen
discussions I've seen over the years in various Usenet groups!)


I'll try to limit myself to just a few of Hal's points:

>Is there really a complexity increase from the AIT point of view?
