>complexity
>that we see.

Sure, in some sense even the "losing" strings have nearly the same
complexity. That's expected, as the winners and losers are playing at
nearly the same level! (The loser is only marginally weaker than the
winner.)

(It's like two heavyweight boxing contenders--they should be fairly evenly
matched by the time they fight.)


>
