>Go.  (It could be that this is true of people as well.)  In Tim's "landscape"
>terms, we might say that it had found a local maximum which missed most of
>the complexity of the game.

Like I said earlier, we'll see how well the GA/GP approach works for Go.
Note that GA/GP has nothing per se to do with the arguments....I could have
used neural nets as the example (in which case the "strings" would be
