         unusably loose for anthropologists.  Cultures can and should
         be distinguished from subcultures by whether the population
         would be self-sufficient if the candidate `parent' culture
         were to vanish.  The Amish were until recently and perhaps
         still are a culture; UNIX hackers are definitely a subculture.

